Z||000000||stingant0||12-16-2001||02:58 AM||||I bought an 88 forumla that didn't run for $900. It is in perfect shape and it is an automatic. The question I have is after I took the engine apart (He never changed the oil--was pennsluge) I noticed he had spun a crank bearing. To turn the crank here is going to be $120 and a new one $215.I have an 87 crank will this fit in with no mods? I know I need an 87 flexplate.||||reg||6
Z||000001||tgowens||12-16-2001||03:14 AM||||No it won't. The '88 is internally balanced with a neutrally balanced flex plate whereas the '87 is not internally balanced and uses a weighted flexplate.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_TGO.jpg">  <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||12-16-2001||09:08 AM||||Terry,<P>If you swap in *both* the 87 crank and flexplate, shouldn't that work? (Might need the 87 harmonic balancer, too.) Aren't the block and all the other internals the same?<P>I'd be surprised if all that's wrong is a spun crank bearing. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||12-16-2001||10:48 AM||||Raydar, I read his post wrong -- you can swap both in but not one without the other.||||reg||1
Z||000004||ray b||12-16-2001||03:45 PM||||3.1 it use a later 3.1 crank to stroke it<BR>will work with 2.8 flex-plate and gives more power some then over bore to get a 3.2 to full 3.4. if it is that gunked up re-bore is needed anyway with new pistons ect.<BR>may as well get all you can, if it is all ready a-part and needs replacement anyway.<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000005||stingant0||12-16-2001||04:28 PM||||The engine is not really that bad. The ONLY problem I saw was the crank, it was REALLY BAD. The cylinder walls look pretty good. You guys should see the oil filter man O man!!! Think of black Jello in a pennsluge filter. I don't want to do any more work then I have to..so the 3.1 is out of question. Yes it is REALLY easy to do and yes I wanted to be mean I guess I could bore it .60 over so the poor guy over heads his engine, but I think I'll just keep it a 2.8. It is an automatic..I hate autos. I need the money from this to help fund my DOHC project <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_drool.gif">  ||||reg||10
